# Day 44

## Experiment Title

Building Docker Images using GitHub Actions


## Objective

To understand how Docker images can be built automatically using GitHub Actions workflows.


## Theory

GitHub Actions can automate the process of creating Docker images whenever changes are pushed to a repository. This process helps developers maintain updated container images without manual intervention.

Docker image automation improves development efficiency and supports Continuous Integration practices. GitHub Actions workflows can execute Docker commands and generate container images automatically during workflow execution.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Docker Desktop

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the GitHub repository.

Access the workflow configuration file.

Configure Docker image build steps inside the workflow.

Commit and push the workflow file to the repository.

Observe the workflow execution process in GitHub Actions.

Verify successful Docker image creation.


## Output

Docker image build automation was configured successfully.

GitHub Actions executed the Docker build process automatically.

The Docker image was created successfully during workflow execution.


## Result

Successfully automated Docker image creation using GitHub Actions.
